/* @catalog — generated by `npm run catalog:generate`; do not edit by hand.
 * Internal
 *   Functions: db, mutation, code, field, request, current, candidatesOf, record, catalogState,
 *              completedReview, run, shownFor, applyShown, answer, featuring, createdRecordId, decideOn,
 *              titleOnlyRun
 *   Constants: actor, other, user, album, artist, first, second, singer, held
 *   Variables: harness, server, base, token, userToken
 * Tests
 *   - candidates and decisions routes guard authentication, the current admin and the viewer, stay private, take 768 KB in any letter case, and decisions replay unlisted
 *   - applying fills Artist entries, the label, member Credits from their own tracks and the expected tracklist, creating and reusing records with their IDs, once across retries
 *   - a decorated primary Artist agrees with a release credited to its first part: applying keeps the Artist and its name, records the release's MusicBrainz ID and needs no decision
 *   - an editor that sends fields only applies them without Credits, records, IDs, tracklist or identity fence
 *   - a name candidate needs an explicit decision, a candidate that appears after the confirmation read shows its row again, and a decided record that changed is stale
 *   - a captured Artist or a member's Artist renamed during the review makes it stale and nothing is written; an ID holder appearing shows the row again, and one not ready is an identity change
 *   - Artist entries and the label take the positions of the Credits they replace, keep every other Credit in order, keep phrases with unchanged successors, and replace the first label
 *   - a first label Credit whose Organization is not ready leaves the label read-only: it is never selected and selecting it is invalid input
 *   - Credits naming one Artist in two letter cases show one entry, so the Album's list is never applied while a title still is; a list captured before that rule is applied only once answered with lookup
 *   - an expected tracklist applies only while every paired member sits at its row after the selected changes, and pairing-filled numbers only with a tracklist that places them
 *   - pairing-filled numbers apply alone against a kept tracklist that places them, and never against one that does not
 *   - member Credits: a conflict kept is never applied and an unanswered one waits; a used one replaces legacy Credits of the Artists it names and keeps every other Credit
 *   - a member whose track credits only a placeholder, or nothing, keeps no Credits even when the Album gains its first primary Artist
 *   - a write failing late in the apply, or Credit writes turned off, leaves no record, ID, Credit, tracklist or receipt behind; the same apply is then admitted once
 *   - the identity candidate read queries 40 Artist names for an import and up to the review's bound when asked
 *   - a track-only artist the catalog keeps under an alias lookup found is a name candidate needing an answer, never a preselected create
 *   - an Album without members takes a chosen candidate's expected tracklist with every row a missing-file row
 *   - records an applied review creates or records an ID on reach listener Artist, Organization, Album and Search responses without a MusicBrainz ID, crediting the Album
 *   - an Album without Artist Credits gains the release's artist as a preselected new Artist, applied over HTTP with an ID derived from the review, the operation and the identity
 *   - a bound identity's Artist keeps the MusicBrainz ID it holds until a decision replaces it, which only that record at its captured revision answers
 *   - bound entries naming different Artists are one conflicting identity: it records no ID, its unbound entry waits for reuse or create, and one list never reuses one Artist twice
 *   - two bound identities recording different IDs on one Artist record none, and a confirmation deselecting either list applies as filtered, recording none either
 *   - an Album list that would name its Artist twice through a member's binding is never offered: no row waits on it, and selecting it is invalid input
 *   - one Artist is created for a name the Album and three members share, and each of them credits it
 *   - one MusicBrainz ID credited under two names creates one Artist named after the Album's entry, and one name under two IDs creates two Artists
 *   - a replaced primary Artist loses the Album while a member still names it; listener Artist and label pages and followed releases follow the new Credits
 *   - identity rows and decisions exist only for a review captured for lookup and not applied; an unreadable capture asks for a reload and a changed source refuses decisions
 *   - selecting a list, label, member or tracklist that equals what the review captured, or an unknown member, is invalid input and writes nothing
 *   - a label named like a saved Organization waits for a decision, and the reused Organization gains the label's MusicBrainz ID and the Album's label Credit
 *   - a rebuilt Album Credit list the Credit rules refuse (more than 50 Credits) is shown but never applied, and nothing is written
 *   - a transient transaction error re-runs the apply against fresh state, which mints each record once with the same ID
 *   - an apply that commits but reports an unknown commit result replays its receipt for the same intent and mints nothing again
 *   - an Album whose Credits name one Artist in two letter cases still applies its title, leaving both Credits as they are
 *   - an identity candidate read past its time budget answers 503 for the confirmation read and the apply, which writes nothing
 *   - a decided replace whose new ID another record took shows its row again; the same set is stale, and a set without it applies with the old ID kept
 *   - a decision set whose identities in two lists reuse one record keeping no ID, each recording its own, is refused; one of them alone is admitted
 *   - a decision naming an identity a candidate choice replaced since the read is stale, never malformed
 *   - a confirmation read while a run was queued is refused once the run wrote other values without changing the review revision, writing nothing
 *   - names the stored run found are read even when the review stored names only for the Album's IDs, as an earlier release did
 *   - an apply racing another identity writer on the fence is retried against fresh state and shows the row again, so no second record is created
 *   - a review keeps its last receipt for applying: other changes stop one receipt early, and the apply is still admitted
 *   - an expected tracklist or pairing-filled numbers are refused while any stored pair cannot be read, writing nothing
 *   - the identity read names its default selection and the Album's kept expected tracklist
 * @end-catalog */

/**
 * Applying an existing-Album review against a MongoDB replica set: the identity rows and decisions an apply of Artist entries and
 * the label waits for, the Credits, records, MusicBrainz IDs and expected tracklist it writes in one transaction, the placement of
 * paired members, member Credits from each member's own paired track, staleness and identity races, that a refusal or a failure
 * writes nothing, that transient retries and unknown commit results mint each record once, and what listener pages, Search and
 * followed releases show afterwards. Lookup runs use fixture MusicBrainz answers. All names, identifiers and accounts are synthetic.
 */
